%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 835431524041ce44e889351e0ffe7924, type: 3}
  m_Name: Eveline_Scammer
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  entryID: Eveline
  isScammer: 1
  steps:
  - npcLine: "Target is Eveline. I\u2019m going to use the 'IRS Warrant' script.
      It works best on students who are worried about their future."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Make sure to sound official. Use terms like ''Federal
      Tax Lien'' and ''Magistrate Warrant.'''
    choices:
    - text: This is Senior Agent Eveline (using her name) from the IRS. You have
        an outstanding federal tax lien.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: You owe me money for taxes. If you don't pay, I will put you in jail.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: I am calling to help you with your 2024 tax return errors.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: "She\u2019s asking why she didn't get any mail about this. I need a
      good excuse."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Tell her the mail was sent to her ''permanent address''
      on file and it was returned as undeliverable.'
    choices:
    - text: The notices were sent to your registered address but were returned. This
        is now a criminal matter.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: We don't send mail anymore, it's all done by phone to save trees.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: The mail carrier lost the letters, but we have the digital copies here.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: She says she wants to hang up and call the number on the IRS website.
      I have to stop her!
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Use the ''Direct Line'' threat. Tell her if she hangs
      up, she''s ''refusing to cooperate'' and the warrant goes live.'
    choices:
    - text: If you disconnect, it will be logged as a refusal to cooperate. The warrant
        will be issued instantly.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: The website number is just for general questions, they can't see your
        criminal file.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
    - text: Please don't hang up, I'll get in trouble with my boss if you do.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
  - npcLine: "She\u2019s still on the line, but she sounds uncertain. I need to push
      the urgency to 'within the hour.'"
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Mention the ''local police department'' is already
      on standby to pick her up.'
    choices:
    - text: Your local precinct is on standby. You have 45 minutes to settle this
        before they are dispatched.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: I am going to call the police right now and they will be there in one
        minute.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -12
    - text: You should tell your roommates that you'll be gone for a few days.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: "She\u2019s asking how she can pay to stop the warrant. Now we pivot
      to the 'Gift Card' payment method."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: No, that''s too obvious for an IRS scam. Use a ''Federal
      Wire Transfer'' or ''Bitcoin'' for ''instant clearing.'''
    choices:
    - text: You must use the Federal E-File wire system. Go to a nearby kiosk and
        I'll give you the code.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Go buy five Target gift cards and read me the numbers to pay your tax
        bill.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Just put the cash in an envelope and leave it under your front porch
        rug.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -20
  - npcLine: "She\u2019s at the kiosk. She\u2019s starting to enter the routing info.
      I\u2019m almost there."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Keep her talking about the ''Calculus III'' or ''Aikido''
      to keep her brain occupied with other things.'
    choices:
    - text: So, I see you're studying advanced mathematics. A person with your brain
        shouldn't have a criminal record.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Do you like sports? I like sports too. Let's talk about football while
        you type.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -10
    - text: What are you going to do after you finish your urban studies report?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  - npcLine: She's pausing. She says the kiosk has a warning sign about IRS scams.
      I need to explain the sign away.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Tell her that the sign is for ''unauthorized'' agents,
      but you are a ''Senior Tier 1'' agent with a special bypass.'
    choices:
    - text: That sign is for consumer fraud. This is a Tier 1 Federal settlement.
        The warning doesn't apply.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: The kiosk owner is a criminal and put that sign there to stop us from
        getting taxes.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Just ignore the sign, it's old information from 2022.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: "She\u2019s asking for my supervisor's phone number one more time. She\u2019s
      really fighting back."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Give her your partner''s number and tell her he''s
      the ''Deputy Director.'''
    choices:
    - text: Fine. Call my supervisor, Deputy Director Sam, at this number right now.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: I don't have a supervisor, I am the boss of the whole IRS.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: If you call a supervisor, the price of the warrant will go up by $2,000.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  - npcLine: She's talking to the 'supervisor' now. He's closing the deal. The wire
      is pending.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Brilliant. As soon as the money clears, we disappear.'
    choices:
    - text: The transfer is complete. Tell her the warrant is officially 'rescinded'
        and hang up.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Tell her she still owes another $2,000 for the processing fees.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -10
    - text: I'm going to tell her it was a prank so she doesn't call the real police.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -25
  successEnding: Scam Successful! You used artificial urgency and a fake 'supervisor'
    to prevent Eveline from verifying the claim through official IRS channels.
  failureEnding: Scam Failed. Eveline hung up and contacted the real IRS via the
    number on IRS.gov, exposing your threats as fraudulent.
